 "parts": [
  "The sticky note began as a glue that failed.",
  "Nineteen sixty-eight. A scientist at 3M, Spencer Silver, wanted a very strong adhesive.",
  "Instead, he made a weak one.",
  "It stuck. But it peeled off without tearing.",
  "In Wikipedia's words, a solution without a problem.",
  "For about five years, few people inside the company cared.",
  "Then a colleague, Arthur Fry, sang in a church choir.",
  "His paper bookmarks kept slipping out of his hymn book.",
  "A gentle grip was exactly what he needed.",
  "Nineteen seventy-seven. A test in several cities. Mixed results.",
  "A year later: free samples in offices in Boise, Idaho.",
  "About nine in ten people who tried them said they would buy.",
  "In nineteen eighty, it went on sale across the United States.",
  "Not everyone agrees on who deserves the credit.",
  "A glue meant to be strong became famous for being weak."
 ],
